% Generate `web/src/studio/model.js`: the pure, dependency-free UI vocabulary + factories + small
% math behind the Studio editor — NO React, NO DOM. The schema-level doc MUTATORS live in
% `../editor/interp.js` (the tested contract core); this file only adds inspector/timeline/preview
% helpers that emit schema-valid fragments. Unit-tested in model.test.js (which pins the exact
% numbers) — keep this prompt to signatures + contracts and let the tests define boundary values.
%
% Two cross-cutting invariants:
%  1. Render-faithful vocab — every offered TRANSITION / anchor / keyframe dim is one the FFmpeg
%     path (tools/video/video_compose.py) actually renders; anything it would drop or degrade to
%     'fade' is NOT offered. The placement helpers mirror the renderer's geometry so preview == export.
%  2. Save-can-never-422 — every factory/preset emits ONLY schema-known keys, so a fragment
%     round-trips through interp.js's `sanitizeOverlay` UNCHANGED (asserted by the tests).

Named exports only (no default). `round3(x)` (round to 3 decimals) and `clamp(x, lo, hi)` are
exported module helpers; `evenDim(n)` = `max(2, round(n/2)*2)` and `centeredAssetPosition` are internal.
All canvas-taking helpers default a missing canvas to 1920×1080.

## Vocabulary constants (exported)
- `TRANSITIONS` — `{value, label}[]` of ONLY the FFmpeg xfade names (offering a non-xfade name would
  silently degrade to fade): `'' Hard cut`, `fade`, `fadeblack` (…through black), `fadewhite`,
  `dissolve`, `wipeleft/right/up/down` (labels `Wipe ←/→/↑/↓`), `slideleft/right` (`Slide ←/→`),
  `circleopen`, `circleclose`, `zoom`.
- `SPEED_PRESETS = [0.5, 1, 1.5, 2, 4]` — quick buttons (FFmpeg renders any positive factor).
- `CANVAS_PRESETS` — `{label, width, height}[]` output canvases, EVEN dims (yuv420p): 9:16 1080×1920,
  1:1 1080×1080, 16:9 1920×1080, 4:5 1080×1350.
- `TEXT_ANCHORS` — the nine drawtext anchors `{top|center|bottom}-{left|center|right}` (center is bare
  `center`), row-major.
- `EASINGS = ['linear','ease-in','ease-out','ease-in-out','spring','step']` (schema enum).
- `KF_DIMS_IMAGE = ['x','y','scale','opacity']`, `KF_DIMS_TEXT = ['x','y','opacity']` — keyframe dims
  the FFmpeg path renders BY overlay kind (rotation is never rendered; text warns+ignores scale).
- `IMAGE_EXTENSIONS = ['.png','.jpg','.jpeg','.bmp','.tiff','.tif','.webp']` — kept in sync with
  video_compose.py `_IMAGE_EXTENSIONS`; `.gif` is intentionally ABSENT (gifs are video-like).
- `AUDIO_LANE_ORDER = ['music','narration','sfx']` — fixed top→bottom timeline sub-lane order.

## Type detection
- `overlayKind(ov)` → `'text' | 'image'` (video counts as image, so `kfDimsFor` is a two-way split):
  explicit `type==='text'` → text; `type` image/video → image; else text IFF it has `text` and no
  `asset_id`, else image.
- `overlayType(ov)` → `'text' | 'image' | 'video'` — the three-way split the inspector/preview need
  (same fallback: text iff `text` and no `asset_id`, else image).
- `kfDimsFor(ov)` → `KF_DIMS_TEXT` for a text overlay else `KF_DIMS_IMAGE`.
- `isImageSource(path)` → true iff the lowercased path ends in an `IMAGE_EXTENSIONS` suffix.
- `clipType(selection, doc)` → the inspector's declarative-schema key for the current selection, or
  null (no selection / no match): a `cut` → `image_main`|`video_main` by `isImageSource(cut.source)`;
  an `overlay` (by `selection.index`) → `text`|`video_overlay`|`image_overlay` via `overlayType`; an
  `audio` selection → its `audioKind` (`music`|`sfx`|`narration`).

## Overlay factories (each returns a complete, CENTERED, schema-valid overlay — feat 4: new overlays
land mid-canvas, then the user drags them; emit only whitelisted keys so `sanitizeOverlay` is a no-op)
- `newTextOverlay({start=0, end=3, track=0})` — `type:'text'`, `text:'Your text'`, `font_size:64`,
  `color:'white'`, `box:{color:'black', opacity:0.5, padding:12}`, round3'd start/end, `position:'center'`
  (a valid drawtext string anchor), `opacity:1`, `track`.
- `newImageOverlay({assetId, start=0, end=3, canvas, track=0})` — `type:'image'`, `asset_id`, an OBJECT
  `position` from `centeredAssetPosition(canvas, 0.3)` (named anchors are text-only), `opacity:1`.
- `newVideoOverlay(...)` — same as image but `type:'video'` and `centeredAssetPosition(canvas, 0.4)`
  (a little larger; PiP audio stays off until toggled via `audio_mix`).
- `centeredAssetPosition(canvas, widthFrac)` (internal) → `{x, y, width}`: `width = round(canvasW*widthFrac)`
  (height stays auto so the renderer keeps aspect); centered assuming a SQUARE box — `x=(W-width)/2`,
  `y=max(0,(H-width)/2)`.

## presetKeyframes(name, ov) → keyframes[] over the overlay's [start,end] window, or null when the
preset doesn't apply. Opacity presets work for ANY kind; MOTION presets need an OBJECT position
(image/video) and return null otherwise. `x`/`y` read from the object position (default 0).
- `fade_in` — opacity 0→1 over the first 0.4s (ease-out).  `fade_out` — 1→0 over the last 0.4s (ease-in).
- `slide_in_left` / `slide_in_right` — x from ±240 (& opacity 0) → resting x (& 1) over ~0.5s, ease-out.
- `pop` — scale 0.6 & opacity 0 → 1 & 1 over ~0.35s, ease-out.
- `ken_burns` — scale 1→1.2 across the whole window (linear).
- unknown name → null. (round3 every keyframe `t`, clamped inside the window.)

## Runtime + audio projections
- `isFfmpeg(doc)` — true when `doc.render_runtime` is missing or `'ffmpeg'` (the studio default).
- `previewAudioTracks(doc)` → the hidden `<audio>` elements for the SOURCE preview: like interp's
  `audioClips` but carrying `volume` and OPEN-ENDED windows. One item per music region (`audio.music`
  as object OR array, legacy top-level `doc.music` as fallback), then narration segments, then sfx;
  skip any with no `asset_id`. Shapes: music `{key:'music'+i, kind:'music', src:asset_id,
  start:max(0,start_seconds||0), end: end_seconds set ? Number : Infinity, volume: volume ?? 1}`;
  narration `{key:'n'+i, kind:'narration', src, start, end: end_seconds set ? Number : Infinity,
  volume:1}`; sfx `{key:'s'+i, kind:'sfx', src, start, end: Infinity, volume: volume ?? 1}`.
- `groupAudioLanes(audioItems=[])` → `[{kind, items}]` grouping a flat audioClips list by kind in
  `AUDIO_LANE_ORDER`, dropping empty kinds (so a full-width music bed and narration segment sit on
  SEPARATE rows instead of occluding each other). `[]` when there's no audio.

## Placement geometry (mirror video_compose.py so preview == export)
- `anchorToXY(anchor, canvas)` → `{x,y,width}` converting a named anchor to an OBJECT for image/video
  overlays (which reject a string anchor). Columns left/center/right at 0.05/0.4/0.7·W, rows
  top/center/bottom at 0.05/0.45/0.85·H, `width = round(0.25·W)`; unknown parts fall back to center.
- `clipFitSize(meta, canvas)` → the main clip's contain-fit box at scale=1: `r = min(cw/sw, ch/sh)`,
  `{round(sw*r), round(sh*r)}`; unknown source dims fall back to the canvas.
- `isScaleObject(scale)` — true iff `scale` is a non-null object (the per-axis box form).
- `scaleAxes(scale=1)` → `{sx, sy}`: a uniform NUMBER → `sx===sy`; an `{x,y}` OBJECT → its axes (each
  defaulting to 1). Any non-finite / non-positive member floors to 1 (a half-formed value can't
  collapse a box to zero). Mirrors the renderer's `_pos_float` split.
- `clipBox(meta, canvas, scale=1)` → `{width, height}`, even dims ≥ 2: a uniform NUMBER → `fit × scale`
  (legacy centered-letterbox box); an `{x,y}` OBJECT → a CANVAS-fraction box `evenDim(cw·sx) ×
  evenDim(ch·sy)` (e.g. `{x:1,y:0.5}` = full-width half-height split panel — the box is the PANEL, the
  clip fits inside it aspect-preserved).
- `clipDefaultPosition(meta, canvas, scale=1)` → the `clipBox` centered on the canvas (top-left `{x,y}`).
- `clipAnchorXY(anchor, meta, canvas, scale=1)` → the `clipBox` flush to a named edge, margin 0 (left→0,
  right→`cw-boxW`, else centered; top→0, bottom→`ch-boxH`, else centered) — flush, unlike the 0.05-margin
  overlay `anchorToXY`.
- `clipPositionXY(cut, meta, canvas)` → `{x,y}` for a cut: an OBJECT `transform.position` (with `x` set)
  as-is; else `clipAnchorXY` on the string anchor (default `'center'`), passing `transform.scale`
  THROUGH so the anchored box uses the right dims.

## Small math
- `round3(x)` — round to 3 decimals.  `clamp(x, lo, hi)`.
- `fmtTime(sec)` → compact `m:ss.c` timecode (one decimal): `m=floor(s/60)`, `r=s-m*60`,
  `` `${m}:${r.toFixed(1).padStart(4,'0')}` ``; clamp negatives/non-numbers to `0:00.0`. (The
  toFixed(1) seam can read as `:60.0` at a tick boundary rather than carrying to the minute — pinned
  by the tests, leave it.)

## Drag-to-scrub number fields (pure math for After-Effects/CapCut-style draggable inputs)
- `decimalsOf(step)` — decimal places implied by `step` (0.05→2, 1→0), 0 for non-finite/≤0, capped at 6.
- `roundTo(x, step)` — round `x` to `decimalsOf(step)` places (kills 0.1+0.2 float noise).
- `scrubValue({start, dx, step=1, min, max, fine=false})` — new value = `start + dx·per` where
  `per = fine ? step/5 : step` (a bad/≤0 step is treated as 1); snap to the `per` grid, clamp to
  `[min,max]` when finite, `roundTo` the result. Tolerant of junk (no NaN leaks).
- `fmtScrub(v)` — compact display: '' for '' / null / non-numbers (= unset/auto), integers bare, else
  trailing zeros dropped.

## summarizeDocChange(prev, next) — the debug recorder's compact prev→next `edit_decisions` diff
Every editor edit funnels through commit/live, so diffing there captures EVERY action as one semantic
event. Returns ONLY what changed (a no-op — same ref or deep-equal — returns `{}`):
`{ cuts?, overlays?, fields? }`. Cap every emitted list at `_MAX_CHANGED = 12`.
- `cuts` — diff by stable `id` (internal `_diffById`): `added`/`removed` id lists, `changed`
  `[{id, fields}]` (fields = keys whose JSON differs), and `reordered:true` when the same id-set is in
  a new order.
- `overlays` — diff by index (internal `_diffByIndex`, no stable id): `count {from,to}` on a length
  change, `changed [{index, fields}]`.
- `fields` — top-level keys other than cuts/overlays whose JSON differs (catches audio / metadata /
  canvas / background / render_runtime).
(Internal `_fieldsChanged(a,b)` returns the keys whose `JSON.stringify` differs across both objects.)
